1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,040
I'm Kai.

2
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:02,080
I drive rideshare.

3
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:05,920
That night, I was three weeks
behind on my rental car,

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,200
I had a hospital bill I'd be
paying off until I was forty,

5
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:12,800
and I'd just found two hundred
thousand dollars in my trunk.

6
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:16,160
A woman on the phone begged
me not to go to the police.

7
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,720
I went anyway.

8
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:20,920
The night desk at the precinct
was pretty much dead.

9
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:25,520
Just one detective, Sharon Bell,
reading glasses pushed up on her head,

10
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,000
and a pot of coffee that smelled burnt.

11
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:31,600
I set the bag on the counter and
told her I'd found it in my car.

12
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:36,360
She unzipped it, looked at the money,
then looked at me for a really long time.

13
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:39,280
"You know most people don't
bring this in, right?"

14
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:42,080
she said. "Found money comes to us.

15
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:43,200
That's the rule.

16
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:46,640
And if the owner shows up, they
usually give the finder a reward.

17
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,480
Sometimes a decent one."

18
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:51,040
Then she called the number
on a report she'd pulled up,

19
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:53,600
said the money had turned
up, and pointed at a chair.

20
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,960
"Sit. This is going to take a while."

21
00:00:57,560 --> 00:01:00,680
I sat in a plastic chair
for forty minutes.

22
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:03,720
Then Detective Bell came
back with a printout.

23
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:05,720
"Your passenger," she said.

24
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:07,040
"Harold Pruitt.

25
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:09,560
They picked him up at
the airport an hour ago.

26
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:13,960
Theft. His employer says he walked off
with two hundred thousand dollars in

27
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:15,440
company cash."

28
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:18,080
So the woman on the phone
wasn't exaggerating.

29
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,720
Her dad was actually going to prison.

30
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:24,320
About ten minutes later, the
door opened, and it was her.

31
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:29,347
Laura. Scrubs, car keys still
in her hand, eyes all red.

32
00:01:29,373 --> 00:01:32,867
"They're bringing my dad in here,"
she told the guy at the front desk.

33
00:01:32,893 --> 00:01:34,280
"I'm his daughter."

34
00:01:34,360 --> 00:01:38,280
Then she turned around and saw the bag on
the detective's desk and just closed her

35
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:39,400
eyes.

36
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:41,680
"You brought it here," she said.

37
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:43,120
She didn't sound mad.

38
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:44,573
Just tired.

39
00:01:44,627 --> 00:01:46,253
She looked at the detective.

40
00:01:46,307 --> 00:01:47,920
"He didn't steal anything.

41
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,120
I swear to you.

42
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:51,240
He was trying to stop something."

43
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:53,800
Detective Bell nodded and wrote it down.

44
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:55,480
She didn't look surprised.

45
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:57,800
I got the feeling she heard that a lot.

46
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:02,507
Detective Bell read the report
out loud, mostly to herself.

47
00:02:02,613 --> 00:02:06,360
"Theft reported by Russell
Brandt, owner of Brandt Markets.

48
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,720
Filed at nine-ten p.m."

49
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:11,280
And something about that bugged me.

50
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:13,320
I pulled up the ride on my phone.

51
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:15,760
Pickup, ten-forty p.m.

52
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,640
I even zoomed in on the time,

53
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:20,680
like it might change if I
stared at it long enough.

54
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:23,880
At nine-ten, Harold wasn't
even in my car yet.

55
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:25,480
He still had the bag.

56
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:28,520
He was still at the office,
waiting for a ride.

57
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:32,080
So how did his boss already
know the money was gone?

58
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:33,320
I looked at Laura.

59
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,720
Laura looked at me.

60
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:36,720
She'd done the same math.

61
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,880
I opened my mouth to say it
out loud, to the detective,

62
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:41,800
to anybody who'd listen.

63
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:44,800
And right then, the door swung open again.

64
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:48,947
A guy in a gray jacket walked
in like he owned the place.

65
00:02:48,973 --> 00:02:51,560
"Name's Vince," he told the detective.

66
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,040
"I'm here for Mister Brandt.

67
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:54,253
The victim."

68
00:02:54,307 --> 00:02:56,720
He put his phone on the
counter, on speaker,

69
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:58,867
and this smooth voice came out.

70
00:02:58,893 --> 00:03:00,320
"Kai, is it?

71
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,520
Russell Brandt.

72
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,840
Listen, I hear you're an honest guy.

73
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:05,040
That's rare.

74
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:07,520
I'd like to give you ten
percent of what you found,

75
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:08,720
as a thank-you.

76
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,960
That's twenty thousand dollars.

77
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,480
All you have to do is sign a statement
that you found the bag in your car,

78
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:17,000
and then go home and get some sleep."

79
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:18,600
Twenty grand.

80
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:20,960
I did the math in about half a second.

81
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,800
Hospital bill, done.

82
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:24,560
Car, done.

83
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,320
Laura was staring at me.

84
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:28,000
So was Detective Bell.

85
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:31,400
And the report on the
desk still said nine-ten.

86
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,200
So there it is.

87
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:36,600
Twenty grand on one side,
nine-ten on the other.

88
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:38,680
If you think I should
tell them everything,

89
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:40,560
tap the video on the left.

90
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:43,800
If I should sign, take the
reward, and stay out of it,

91
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:45,360
tap the one on the right.

92
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:48,000
And you can always come back
and try the other path.
